// Practice quiz: A GitHub Actions pipeline: tests, then image builds
// Unreviewed first draft, 2026-11-04. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: containers-cicd/microservices-and-ci-cd/github-actions-pipeline

::o1 on::In a workflow file, which key says what starts a run? {
~runs-on#Not quite. That chooses the runner.
=on#Correct. on lists the triggering events.
~needs#Not quite. That sets job dependencies.
~steps#Not quite. That lists what a job does.
}

::o1 runner::What does runs-on\: ubuntu-latest choose? {
~The Docker base image in your Dockerfile#Not quite. FROM in the Dockerfile sets that.
~The branch that triggers the run#Not quite. That belongs under on.
=The machine image the job runs on#Correct. It selects the runner.
~The order of the steps#Not quite. Steps run in the order they are written.
}

::o2 needs::Job deploy has needs\: build, and build fails. What happens to deploy? {
~It runs anyway#Not quite. Only a conditional such as always() would allow that.
~It runs first#Not quite. needs makes it wait, not lead.
~It retries build#Not quite. needs does not retry anything.
=It is skipped#Correct. A failed dependency skips the jobs that need it.
}

::o2 default::Two jobs have no needs. How do they run by default? {
~In file order#Not quite. File order sets no dependency.
~Alphabetically#Not quite. Names do not set order.
~One per day#Not quite. That has nothing to do with job scheduling.
=In parallel#Correct. Jobs run in parallel unless told otherwise.
}

::o3 checkout::Why does a build job with context\: . need actions/checkout first? {
=The runner starts without your repository files#Correct. A path context reads files from the runner.
~It installs Docker#Not quite. Checkout only fetches the repository.
~It signs the image#Not quite. Checkout does not sign anything.
~It pushes the image#Not quite. That is the build action's job.
}

::o3 push::A build step has push\: false. What is true after it succeeds? {
~The image is in the registry#Not quite. That needs push\: true.
=The image was built, and no registry received it#Correct. Building and pushing are separate.
~Nothing was built#Not quite. The build still ran.
~The tests were skipped#Not quite. That setting does not affect tests.
}
